SERENITY UAV — DEFERRED PHASES LICENSING
=========================================

**Hardware Designs:** CERN Open Hardware License v2 — Weakly Reciprocal (CERN-OHL-W)

**Documentation:** CC BY 4.0 (Creative Commons Attribution)

See root LICENSE and docs/attribution_and_licensing.md for full details:
  ../LICENSE
  ../docs/attribution_and_licensing.md

---

SUMMARY (Deferred Phases)

Phase 11+ design files (aft EDF integration, cargo-bay range-extender battery,
and speculative future features) follow the same dual-licensing model as the
baseline Serenity UAV hardware:

  • CAD files, STLs, schematics → CERN-OHL-W (reciprocal open hardware)
  • Design documentation, specifications → CC BY 4.0 (permissive attribution)

Even though these phases are deferred pending flight-test validation, they are
licensed identically to Phases 0–10.

---

PHASE-SPECIFIC FILES

**Phase 11 — Aft EDF Integration:**
  aft-edf/*.stl, *.FCStd           — CERN-OHL-W (CAD geometry)
  rcs-thrusters/*.stl, *.FCStd     — CERN-OHL-W (RCS manifold design)
  README.md, WBS.md, TODO.md       — CC BY 4.0 (documentation)

**Phase 12 — Cargo-Bay Battery Module:**
  cargo-rbm/*.stl, *.FCStd         — CERN-OHL-W (gondola & tray CAD)
  README.md, WBS.md                — CC BY 4.0 (documentation)

**Phase 13+ — Speculative:**
  design documentation             — CC BY 4.0 (future exploration)
  (CAD, if created, will be CERN-OHL-W)

